  "narrative": "All estimates are interpreted as already signed to the claimed hypothesis direction and judged against the 0.15 composite-dependency-unit threshold. H110 is the most important new result: PTEN loss versus intact among TP53-intact and MSI-nonhigh samples has signed estimate +0.2817 with interval +0.1899 to +0.3735 and adequate cells (199 exposed, 1289 comparator). The entire interval is above the threshold in the PTEN-loss stronger-dependency direction, so I accept it. This is a broader but still conditional PTEN context, less nested than already accepted and validated clean central-intact contexts such as H97, and it directly tests the main uncertainty around PTEN after earlier TP53-intact evidence. I keep it active and request independent validation because validation is the best way to assess whether this common TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh PTEN association is robust within this dataset. H114 through H117 also support robustness of the central predictors outside MSI-high. SMARCA4 loss remains strongly associated with stronger dependency in high aneuploidy_score samples excluding MSI-high (+0.7960 [0.6481, 0.9439]) and in high mutation_burden samples excluding MSI-high (+0.7283 [0.5587, 0.8979]). TP53 loss remains associated with weaker dependency in high aneuploidy_score samples excluding MSI-high (+0.4616 [0.2703, 0.6529]), and KEAP1 loss remains associated with weaker dependency in the same context (+0.8639 [0.7259, 1.0019]). All four full intervals clear the threshold in the registered directions, so I accept and close them as dataset-internal robustness evidence. H91 shows MSI-high remains associated with stronger dependency within SMARCA4-loss cells (+0.6355 [0.4479, 0.8231]), with a full interval above threshold, so I accept and close it, noting the exposed cell is small (29) and the interval is somewhat wide. This is consistent with MSI-high being robust across central predictor backgrounds. The interaction architecture remains largely unsupported at the threshold level. H111 tests TP53-loss by KEAP1-loss interaction restricted to MSI-nonhigh samples; the signed estimate is +0.1382 with interval -0.0565 to +0.3329. The point is below threshold and the interval includes zero, so I reject this registered interaction. This weakens the earlier suggestive H102 TP53-by-KEAP1 interaction, and I move H102 from active to deferred because the MSI-restricted refinement did not clear the threshold. H112 tests SMARCA4-loss by lineage interaction restricted to MSI-nonhigh samples; the signed estimate is +0.2146 with interval +0.0656 to +0.3636. The point exceeds threshold, but the lower bound remains below threshold, and this resembles the earlier unrefined H78 result. I therefore leave H112 unresolved and defer further investigation; I also defer H78 because H112 does not resolve the interaction. H113 tests MSI-high by TP53-loss interaction; the signed estimate is +0.1235 with wide interval -0.3163 to +0.5633. The exposed MSI-high/TP53-loss cell is small (24), and the result is below threshold and imprecise, so I leave it unresolved and deferred rather than closing as a precise null. H95 tests MSI-high by lineage subtype interaction; the signed estimate is -0.1760 with interval -0.4351 to +0.0831. It is not consistently meaningful in the claimed direction and includes zero, so I reject and close it. Overall, the dataset-internal map strengthens: SMARCA4 loss, MSI-high, TP53 loss, and KEAP1 loss effects are robust across genomic-instability contexts; MSI-high remains associated with stronger dependency even within SMARCA4-loss cells; PTEN loss now has a new accepted TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh conditional association pending independent validation. Interaction evidence remains weak, with only H110 receiving validation because it most directly clarifies the remaining PTEN boundary. All conclusions are descriptive and dataset-internal, not causal, not single-gene knockout specificity for the composite endpoint, and not evidence of external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 9 appraise: New central robustness results H114-H117 accepted and closed: SMARCA4 loss effect persists in high aneuploidy_score and high mutation_burden nonMSI contexts; TP53 and KEAP1 effects persist in high aneuploidy nonMSI. MSI-high accepted within SMARCA4-loss cells H91 despite small exposed n=29. H95 MSI-by-lineage interaction rejected. Interaction map remains weak: H111 MSI-nonhigh TP53-by-KEAP1 rejected; H102 deferred. H112 MSI-nonhigh SMARCA4-by-lineage near-threshold unresolved deferred; H78 deferred. H113 MSI-by-TP53 interaction unresolved deferred due small exposed cell and wide interval. PTEN map: H110 PTEN loss in TP53-intact and MSI-nonhigh accepted (+0.2817 [0.1899,0.3735]) and selected for validation as highest-priority unresolved PTEN boundary. PTEN remains conditional globally; do not overgeneralize to all samples. If H110 validation clears threshold, PTEN-loss stronger dependency is supported in a broader common TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh context; if validation interval crosses threshold, PTEN remains conditional and global PTEN remains uncertain. Avoid further near-threshold PTEN context mining unless H110 validation materially changes the map. All claims remain dataset-internal descriptive associations.",
  "validate": "H110"
}

