  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the claimed hypothesis direction, and the practical threshold is 0.15 composite dependency-score units. H104 is assessed at its validation deadline. PTEN loss versus intact in the highly selected clean context of adenocarcinoma, MSI-nonhigh, SMARCA4-intact, TP53-intact, and KEAP1-intact cells had discovery estimate +0.279 [0.186, 0.373] and independent validation +0.203 [0.073, 0.333]. The validation point estimate is in the same PTEN-loss stronger-dependency direction and has meaningful magnitude, but the very conservative validation lower bound does not clear the threshold. I therefore maintain acceptance as a discovery-supported conditional association in this dataset and close it, with the caveat that validation supports rather than independently confirms the threshold in that selected context. H110 is the key new PTEN result. PTEN loss versus intact among TP53-intact and MSI-nonhigh samples had discovery +0.282 [0.190, 0.374] and independent validation +0.275 [0.143, 0.406]. The discovery evidence fully cleared the threshold, and validation is highly consistent in point estimate and direction. The validation lower bound is only slightly below 0.15, so independent confirmation of the threshold is not strict, but the result strongly supports PTEN-loss stronger dependency in this broader, less nested TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh context. I accept and close H110. Together with H62, H66, H68, H80, H97, and H104, the PTEN map remains conditional: PTEN-loss stronger dependency is most evident when TP53 is intact and/or in MSI-nonhigh and clean central-intact backgrounds, while global PTEN remains unresolved. I mark near-threshold PTEN single-context claims H60, H64, H86, and H96 deferred rather than continuing to mine similar near-boundary contexts without new information. The current supported dataset-internal map is: SMARCA4 loss is robustly associated with stronger composite dependency, with independent validation and robustness in high aneuploidy and high non-MSI mutation-burden contexts; MSI-high is robustly associated with stronger composite dependency, with independent validation and persistence across SMARCA4-loss/intact, TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, lineage, and clean contexts; TP53 loss is robustly associated with weaker composite dependency, with independent validation and robustness in high-aneuploidy non-MSI contexts; KEAP1 loss is very strongly associated with weaker composite dependency in discovery and many subgroup contexts, but global independent validation remains pending. I leave H14 active because it is the highest-priority remaining central validation target. Negative or nonmeaningful findings include all constructed research markers and their signature interactions, most conventional driver or marker associations after the EGFR/BRAF screen, STK11, MTAP, BRCA2, RB1, NF1, SMAD4, APC, ERBB2, PIK3CA, MYC amplification, sex, media-serum contrasts, CRISPR-library or matched-omics availability effects, and most effect-modifier interactions. The central association map remains largely additive, with unresolved or rejected interactions including TP53-by-SMARCA4, KEAP1-by-SMARCA4, PTEN-by-SMARCA4/TP53/KEAP1/lineage/QC, MSI-by-lineage, MSI-by-TP53, SMARCA4-by-lineage, and TP53-by-KEAP1 variants. Unresolved scientific uncertainty is concentrated in global PTEN, several near-threshold PTEN contexts, PTEN within SMARCA4-loss after inconsistent validation, and a few interactions or central robustness checks. The most informative next analysis is independent validation of H14 global KEAP1 loss. The newly registered robustness comparisons are also useful: PTEN loss in TP53-intact, MSI-nonhigh, high-aneuploidy samples tests whether the accepted PTEN context survives chromosomal instability, while KEAP1 and TP53 loss in high non-MSI mutation burden complete central robustness in genomic-instability backgrounds. All conclusions remain descriptive, dataset-internal, noncausal, not specific to a single-gene knockout mechanism, and not evidence of external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 9 synthesize: H110 PTEN in TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh accepted/closed after validation +0.275 [0.143,0.406], point stable and lower slightly below threshold. H104 accepted/closed, validation +0.203 [0.073,0.333] supports direction but is selected and does not clear independent threshold. PTEN remains conditional; global PTEN unresolved. Defer near-threshold PTEN contexts H60/H64/H86/H96 to avoid redundant boundary mining. Prioritize remaining validation request on H14 global KEAP1-loss; mark H14 active. Registered robustness proposals: PTEN loss in TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh/high aneuploidy; KEAP1 and TP53 loss in high non-MSI mutation burden. If selected, these complete central robustness and test PTEN chromosomal-instability context. All claims remain dataset-internal descriptive associations."
